---
// How Jiji relates to jj itself, and what it sends over the network. HN
// readers ask both first; every line here must stay literally true.
---

<section class="band" id="compat">
  <div class="container cols">
    <div>
      <h2>Works with the jj you have</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Built on jj-lib 0.45</dt>
        <dd>
          Same repository format and config as <code>jj</code> 0.45: your
          <code>trunk()</code>, <code>immutable_heads()</code>, revset aliases and merge tools
          apply as they do in the CLI. The <code>jj</code> binary itself is optional.
        </dd>
        <dt>Next to the terminal</dt>
        <dd>
          A file watcher picks up edits and operations from your terminal as they happen, and
          <code>jj op log</code> shows everything Jiji did. <code>jj undo</code> works on it.
        </dd>
        <dt>Git repositories too</dt>
        <dd>
          Open a plain Git repository and Jiji offers to set jj up in it, the way
          <code>jj git init --colocate</code> does. Git keeps working alongside.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>No telemetry</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Your Git remotes</dt>
        <dd>
          A <code>git fetch</code> when you open a repository and then every 15 minutes
          (adjustable, or off). Pushes happen only when you ask.
        </dd>
        <dt>GitHub</dt>
        <dd>
          Only for publishing and pull requests, with a token you provide or
          <code>gh auth token</code>. Tokens live in the macOS Keychain.
        </dd>
        <dt>Updates and licensing</dt>
        <dd>
          An update check against GitHub Releases, which downloads in the background and waits
          for you to restart. A license key, if you enter one, is validated with Polar at most
          once a day.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 64px);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-5);
  }

  dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-top: var(--sp-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--clr-border-2);
  }

  dd {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--clr-text-2);
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
